No, I think not. Because I don't consider wishes to be only existing to
fix one (quasi-)instant death source (in cases you haven't found another
source for that resistance). I'd rather see wishes also as a means to
(somewhat) compensate the extreme variances in object generation that I
observed in my games, and to avoid any resulting boring processes to
obtain those objects by other means, or to get stuck otherwise. That's
for the advanced players (post Castle). Early random wishes (from rare
and dangerous sources) serve another purpose for newbies, of course.
Wishes as they are presently existing serve all ranks of players in
different (and IMO balanced) ways; that's quite notable for a design
detail yet as powerful as wishes are occasionally considered, and which
are, OTOH, often considered not even necessary to ascend by advanced
players in most games (resulting even in two conducts related to wishes).

